<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions bonds worth 25.33 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions bonds worth 25.33 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned six-month maturity short term federal bonds worth 25.33 billion rupees ($627.8 million) on Tuesday at a weighted average yield of 16.05251 percent per annum.</p>
<p>The bank recieved bids worth a total of 25.77 billion rupees out of which bids for 25.33 billion rupees were accepted.</p>
<p>In a previous auction held on June 3, bids worth 9.37 billion rupees were accepted at a weighted average yield of 16.39886 percent per annum.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192 ($ = 40.34 Pakistani Rupees)</p>
